{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794381737811,"sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","part":{"id":"prt_1c97c6f1f0014ypHD4WLomte55","messageID":"msg_1c97c5608001FoxfhmoFrcbn0p","sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794381737812,"sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","part":{"id":"prt_1c97c6f230012pqUVHIPRMpXm1","messageID":"msg_1c97c5608001FoxfhmoFrcbn0p","sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","type":"text","text":"<think>Let me check the git log and the requirements.lock to see what's available. I need to decide on dependencies:\n\nBackend:\n- Flask (already)\n- Need SQLite — Python 3.13 has sqlite3 in stdlib. I could use raw sqlite3 to avoid adding dependencies. That's probably the simplest and most robust — avoid network installs. Let me check the requirements.lock to see what's there.\n- Password hashing: werkzeug.security (comes with Flask) has generate_password_hash and check_password_hash. \n- Tokens: could use `itsdangerous` (a Flask dependency) for signing tokens. Let me check the lock file.\n\nFrontend:\n- React + TypeScript + Vite already. Need Tailwind CSS. Tailwind v4 with @tailwindcss/vite plugin. Need to install via npm - is network available? The sandbox \"can install packages from the public package registries (through a read-only cache)\". Let me check npm cache.\n\nLet me check the lock file contents first.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794381737763,"end":1794381737805}}}
