{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794381744128,"sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","part":{"id":"prt_1c97c87d5001gNZWMmjos0AoWl","messageID":"msg_1c97c6fb500156SOMT1Wr4JCuE","sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794381744129,"sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","part":{"id":"prt_1c97c87d9001wnJ60OvHjIuct6","messageID":"msg_1c97c6fb500156SOMT1Wr4JCuE","sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","type":"text","text":"<think>Good. `itsdangerous` is available as a Flask dependency. I can use `itsdangerous` URLSafeTimedSerializer for tokens, or just use Python's `hmac`/`hashlib` with stdlib. Actually simplest: use `itsdangerous` since it's already installed (Flask depends on it). But relying on a transitive dependency is a bit iffy; I can add `itsdangerous==2.2.0` to requirements.txt explicitly.\n\nFor SQLite: use stdlib `sqlite3`. That avoids adding SQLAlchemy dependency. Let me check if flask-sqlalchemy is in lock... no. So stdlib sqlite3 it is.\n\nNow, let me check npm availability for Tailwind. Let me test npm registry access.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794381744089,"end":1794381744123}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794381744907,"sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-430142eb-5e9f-4a2a-a06c-02b54a91e082","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 --version; pip --version; python3 -c \"import flask, itsdangerous, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\" 2>&1","workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"Python 3.13.5\npip 25.1.1 from /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pip (python 3.13)\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, itsdangerous, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\n","metadata":{"output":"Python 3.13.5\npip 25.1.1 from /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pip (python 3.13)\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, itsdangerous, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 --version; pip --version; python3 -c \"import flask, itsdangerous, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\" 2>&1","time":{"start":1794381744115,"end":1794381744904}},"id":"prt_1c97c87ed001gk3LdsvHAoU1Rp","sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","messageID":"msg_1c97c6fb500156SOMT1Wr4JCuE"}}
