{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794381846643,"sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","part":{"id":"prt_1c97e1859001NKMkxRYzE5HToz","messageID":"msg_1c97e05fb001DYdpaZqQnZeY2Z","sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794381846643,"sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","part":{"id":"prt_1c97e185c001JFPPXojGsc5Ocl","messageID":"msg_1c97e05fb001DYdpaZqQnZeY2Z","sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","type":"text","text":"<think>No typescript in the lock. Vite 8 can build .tsx files without TypeScript installed (esbuild transpile). But for type checking and editor support, adding typescript + @types/react + @types/react-dom is good practice. The README says dependencies are pinned via package-lock; I'll update the lock with npm install.\n\nLet me install: tailwindcss@4, @tailwindcss/vite, typescript, @types/react, @types/react-dom.\n\nAlso add scripts: \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\", \"build\": \"tsc -b && vite build\" maybe. Since instructions say run lint and typecheck commands if provided — none provided; I'll add typecheck script and run it.\n\nLet's do the install now (network available).</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794381846620,"end":1794381846639}}}
