{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794382292133,"sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-316b3795-aca6-4fcc-b228-d3c168ab90a8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":".venv/bin/pip install --quiet --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock && .venv/bin/python -c \"import flask, itsdangerous, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\"","timeout":300000,"workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"ERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\n","metadata":{"output":"ERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":".venv/bin/pip install --quiet --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock && .venv/bin/python -c \"import flask, itsdangerous, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\"","time":{"start":1794382291580,"end":1794382292116}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c984e277001l47bxgwNsuq7I6","sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","messageID":"msg_1c984d4bf0