{"type":"text","timestamp":1794382557810,"sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","part":{"id":"prt_1c988f263001VpJVtedcX64yWF","messageID":"msg_1c988dbda001FWlmH3NNRZFotM","sessionID":"ses_e3683fd44ffeu9mw9DmUwiGHZw","type":"text","text":"<think>Almost everything passes. Two failures:\n1. \"admin login\" — the test sends `{\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": admin_password}` where admin_password came from os.environ of the *test* process (not set) → empty password → 400. My test's fault: the env var wasn't passed to the test process. Let me fix the test to use \"adminpass\".\n2. \"frontend served\" — no frontend build yet (expected).\n\nLet me fix the test and re-run with ADMIN_PASSWORD set for the test process.\n\nNote: the admin account exists in the DB (created at startup with the password) — login as admin should work. Let me verify.\n\nLet me update the test to use a fixed admin password and pass ADMIN_PASSWORD=adminpass when running the test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794382557795,"end":1794382557808}}}
